<title>ISRAEL: Israel, South Korea to set up research fund.</title>
<headline>Israel, South Korea to set up research fund.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1997-07-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Israel and South Korea have agreed to set up a $6 million industrial research and development fund to encourage joint ventures, Israel's Industry and Trade Ministry said on Sunday.</p>
<p>The fund, with a lifespan of three years, will provide grants for joint projects and encourage joint ventures between Israeli and Korean companies, the ministry said.</p>
<p>The decision was made in Jerusalem during a four-day visit of a South Korean delegation organised by the Korean Ministry of Industry, Trade and Energy. The ministry did not give a timetable for the setting up of the fund.</p>
<p>Israel already has similar funds with the United States, Canada and Singapore.</p>
<p>- Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211</p>
